{"schemaVersion":1,"workId":"OL74502W","title":"The Iron Heel","authors":["Jack London"],"firstPublished":1907,"edition":{"description":"Sections as detected in Project Gutenberg eBook #1164.","source":"Project Gutenberg eBook #1164","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1164"},"sectionLabel":{"singular":"Chapter","plural":"Chapters"},"sections":[{"id":"s1","label":"Ch. 1","title":"MY EAGLE"},{"id":"s2","label":"Ch. 2","title":"CHALLENGES"},{"id":"s3","label":"Ch. 3","title":"JACKSON’S ARM"},{"id":"s4","label":"Ch. 4","title":"SLAVES OF THE MACHINE"},{"id":"s5","label":"Ch. 5","title":"THE PHILOMATHS"},{"id":"s6","label":"Ch. 6","title":"ADUMBRATIONS"},{"id":"s7","label":"Ch. 7","title":"THE BISHOP’S VISION"},{"id":"s8","label":"Ch. 8","title":"THE MACHINE BREAKERS"},{"id":"s9","label":"Ch. 9","title":"THE MATHEMATICS OF A DREAM"},{"id":"s10","label":"Ch. 10","title":"THE VORTEX"},{"id":"s11","label":"Ch. 11","title":"THE GREAT ADVENTURE"},{"id":"s12","label":"Ch. 12","title":"THE BISHOP"},{"id":"s13","label":"Ch. 13","title":"THE GENERAL STRIKE"},{"id":"s14","label":"Ch. 14","title":"THE BEGINNING OF THE END"},{"id":"s15","label":"Ch. 15","title":"LAST DAYS"},{"id":"s16","label":"Ch. 16","title":"THE END"},{"id":"s17","label":"Ch. 17","title":"THE SCARLET LIVERY"},{"id":"s18","label":"Ch. 18","title":"IN THE SHADOW OF SONOMA"},{"id":"s19","label":"Ch. 19","title":"TRANSFORMATION"},{"id":"s20","label":"Ch. 20","title":"A LOST OLIGARCH"},{"id":"s21","label":"Ch. 21","title":"THE ROARING ABYSMAL BEAST"},{"id":"s22","label":"Ch. 22","title":"THE CHICAGO COMMUNE"},{"id":"s23","label":"Ch. 23","title":"THE PEOPLE OF THE ABYSS"},{"id":"s24","label":"Ch. 24","title":"NIGHTMARE"},{"id":"s25","label":"Ch. 25","title":"THE TERRORISTS"}],"groups":[{"id":"g-everhard","label":"Everhard (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"ernest-everhard","name":"Ernest Everhard","aliases":["Ernest"],"role":"protagonist","group":"g-everhard","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “[1] The Second Revolt was largely the work of Ernest Everhard, though he coöperated, of course, with the European leaders.”"},{"id":"iron-heel","name":"Iron Heel","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Woe to the Iron Heel!”"},{"id":"bishop-morehouse","name":"Bishop Morehouse","aliases":["Bishop"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “I know that I could not avoid dropping my eyes, and I was quite relieved when I passed him on and turned to greet Bishop Morehouse—a favorite of mine, a sweet and serious man of middle age, Christ-like in appearance a…”"},{"id":"united-states","name":"United States","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “It is on record that Theodore Roosevelt, at that time President of the United States, said in 1905 A.D., in his address at Harvard Commencement: “_We all know that, as things actually are, many of the most influential…”"},{"id":"oligarchy","name":"Oligarchy","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “[5] Originally, they were private detectives; but they quickly became hired fighting men of the capitalists, and ultimately developed into the Mercenaries of the Oligarchy.”"},{"id":"jackson","name":"Jackson","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““That man’s name is Jackson,” Ernest said.”"},{"id":"wickson","name":"Wickson","aliases":["Mr. Wickson"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “I saw Mr.”"},{"id":"dr-hammerfield","name":"Dr. Hammerfield","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““Go on,” they urged, and Dr.”"},{"id":"mr-calvin","name":"Mr. Calvin","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “There was one other man who was quizzed by Ernest at this juncture, a Mr.”"},{"id":"hartman","name":"Hartman","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s22","summary":"First mention: “Among the travellers in my Pullman was comrade Hartman, like myself in the secret service of the Iron Heel.”"},{"id":"garthwaite","name":"Garthwaite","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s23","summary":"First mention: ““I’m Garthwaite.””"},{"id":"colonel-van-gilbert","name":"Colonel Van Gilbert","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “At the head of the room, Miss Brentwood introduced him to Colonel Van Gilbert, and I knew that the latter was to preside.”"},{"id":"biedenbach","name":"Biedenbach","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s18","summary":"First mention: “Comrade Biedenbach did not betray the Cause.”"},{"id":"avis-everhard","name":"Avis Everhard","role":"minor","group":"g-everhard","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “[3] With all respect to Avis Everhard, it must be pointed out that Everhard was but one of many able leaders who planned the Second Revolt.”"},{"id":"sierra-mills","name":"Sierra Mills","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““I understand you have money, or your father has, which is the same thing—money invested in the Sierra Mills.””"},{"id":"colonel-ingram","name":"Colonel Ingram","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““Colonel Ingram is leading counsel for the company.”"},{"id":"mr-asmunsen","name":"Mr. Asmunsen","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “There were both partners of the big drug firm of Kowalt & Washburn, and Mr.”"},{"id":"grangers","name":"Grangers","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “Yet they were more fortunate than the Grangers, who captured a dozen state governments, and who, in the spring, were not permitted to take possession of the captured offices.”"},{"id":"peter-donnelly","name":"Peter Donnelly","aliases":["Donnelly"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““Why did you not call attention to the fact that Jackson was trying to save the machinery from being injured?” I asked Peter Donnelly, one of the foremen who had testified at the trial.”"},{"id":"mr-kowalt","name":"Mr. Kowalt","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “Ernest turned abruptly on Mr.”"},{"id":"john-carlson","name":"John Carlson","aliases":["Carlson"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s18","summary":"First mention: “Before I go on I want to say a word for this comrade, John Carlson, a humble figure of the Revolution, one of the countless faithful ones in the ranks.”"},{"id":"miss-brentwood","name":"Miss Brentwood","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “It was the creation of Miss Brentwood, an enormously wealthy old maid; and it was her husband, and family, and toy.”"},{"id":"rockefeller","name":"Rockefeller","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “[6] Standard Oil and Rockefeller—see footnote [10]”"},{"id":"hearst","name":"Hearst","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “One great factor that helped to swell the socialist vote was the destruction of Hearst.[1] This the Plutocracy found an easy task.”"},{"id":"pervaise","name":"Pervaise","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “A little less than a hundred years ago, and a little more than six hundred years after her death, the confession of Pervaise was discovered in the secret archives of the Vatican.”"},{"id":"anna-roylston","name":"Anna Roylston","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s18","summary":"First mention: “Of the other two, Bertha Stole disappeared twelve years later, while Anna Roylston still lives and plays an increasingly important part in the Revolution.[3]”"},{"id":"mr-everhard","name":"Mr. Everhard","role":"minor","group":"g-everhard","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “I refer to Mr.”"},{"id":"dr-ballingford","name":"Dr. Ballingford","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““Yet the thought of Aristotle ruled Europe for twelve centuries,” Dr.”"},{"id":"mr-owen","name":"Mr. Owen","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “He began with Mr.”"},{"id":"connor","name":"Connor","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “O’Connor, the president of the Association of Machinists, had been foremost of the six leaders present in refusing to give such assurance.”"},{"id":"asgard","name":"Asgard","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “In the great museum at Asgard there is a book entitled “Essays in Application,” written by Henry van Dyke.”"},{"id":"mrs-pertonwaithe","name":"Mrs. Pertonwaithe","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Wickson and Mrs.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"avis-everhard","target":"iron-heel","weight":5,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r2","source":"avis-everhard","target":"ernest-everhard","weight":9,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r3","source":"bishop-morehouse","target":"ernest-everhard","weight":59,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":4,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":29},{"at":"s7","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","weight":44}]},{"id":"r4","source":"ernest-everhard","target":"mr-everhard","weight":4,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":2,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r5","source":"dr-hammerfield","target":"ernest-everhard","weight":31,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":26}]},{"id":"r6","source":"dr-ballingford","target":"ernest-everhard","weight":6,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":4,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."}]},{"id":"r7","source":"dr-ballingford